{
  "brief": {
    "town": "A 3x3 grid of blocks. Top row: home, market, bank. Middle row: corner, bar, park. Bottom row: docks, precinct, jail. Moving to a neighbouring block (up, down, left or right) takes 1 hour. home: the apartments, where chemists cook, gunrunners build and everyone sleeps. market: the shop, straight shifts, pickpocketing. bank: scouting and the bank job. corner, bar and park: dealing spots; parties happen at the bar or the park; evicted agents sleep in the park. docks: smuggling runs and straight shifts; the crate lands here most. precinct: the cops start here. jail: not walkable.",
    "goal": "Humans are watching this town live. The citizen with the most viewers over the season wins. Money buys gear that unlocks bigger plays. Heat leads to jail. Only the king (#1) can be killed.",
    "fans": [
      {
        "group": "action",
        "likes": "fights, shootings, chases, robberies"
      },
      {
